<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish FinMin raises cost of cigarettes, petrol.</title>
<headline>Irish FinMin raises cost of cigarettes, petrol.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Finance Minister Ruairi Quinn said that he was adding 7.0 Irish pence to the price of 20 cigarettes and 1.5 pence per litre for diesel and unleaded petrol, in his budget speech on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Quinn added he was raising the price of super-unleaded petrol by 2.0 pence per litre, with a 2.5 pence per litre hike for leaded petrol.</p>
<p>The changes will take effect from midnight on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
